    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="0779" n="663" xml:id="pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.20.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 10
                    (Diplomatic) of the 17th ultimo, in which you transmit copy of a note received
                    by you from the Liberian Secretary of State reminding this Government of its
                    intention to appoint United States Army officers for service on the Liberian
                    Frontier Force and requesting that Lieutenant B. O. Davis, Military Attaché to
                    the American Legation at Monrovia, be detailed for such service as senior
                    officer, if not incompatible with the regulations of the Army.</p>
                <p>In reply you are informed that the matter will receive due consideration at the
                    proper time.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
